# Copy this file to .env and fill in your database connection string.
# .env is ignored by git, so your password stays on this computer.
#
# Supabase: dashboard -> your project -> Connect -> "Session pooler" -> URI.
# Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with your database password. If the password has
# symbols like @ : / # ?, either change it to letters and digits or URL-encode them.
#
# Leave DATABASE_URL unset to keep short links in memory only.
